# Hourly backup + free-space monitor — alerts to Slack when either goes wrong.
#
# !! THIS FILE IS NOT DEPLOYED. !!
# Deploys update /srv/hybridInference/ops/db/check-backup-health.sh but never
# touch /etc/cron.d/freeinference-backup-health, which is installed by hand.
# Editing the schedule or the thresholds here changes NOTHING in production
# until someone re-runs the install command below. Anything that has to take
# effect without that step belongs in check-backup-health.sh, not here.
#
# Install / update: sudo cp ops/db/backup-health-cron /etc/cron.d/freeinference-backup-health
#                   sudo chmod 644 /etc/cron.d/freeinference-backup-health
# Verify what is actually live: sudo cat /etc/cron.d/freeinference-backup-health
#
# Requires: AWS credentials in ~freeinference/.aws/credentials (to list the
#           backup bucket) and read access to /srv/hybridInference/.env (to
#           resolve the Slack webhook). The freeinference group has both.
#
# Why hourly, and why it watches S3 rather than the backup log:
#   backup.sh reports a run that started and then broke. It cannot report a run
#   that never fired, or one that "succeeded" with a truncated dump — both of
#   which have happened and gone unnoticed for days. Only something outside the
#   job can catch those, so this reads the uploaded objects instead: their age
#   covers "never ran", their size covers "ran but wrote nothing".
#
# Alert thresholds (override with flags on the command below):
#   backup older than 26h        — the 04:00 job plus a 2h grace for a long dump
#   backup under 50% of largest  — a truncated dump that still uploaded cleanly
#   free space under 80 GiB      — Postgres and the dump share this volume
#
# Repeat alerts for the same condition are suppressed for 6h, so a days-long
# problem does not post 24 identical messages a day. Recovery clears it.
#
# Verify the alert path end to end (posts a test message to Slack):
#   sudo -u freeinference /srv/hybridInference/ops/db/check-backup-health.sh --test

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
HOME=/home/freeinference

20 * * * * freeinference /srv/hybridInference/ops/db/check-backup-health.sh >> /home/freeinference/backup-health.log 2>&1
